[32m+[m[32m## Installation[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mUse Python 3.11. From the project folder, create and activate a virtual environment.[m
[32m+[m[32mFor Windows PowerShell:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```powershell[m
[32m+[m[32mpython -m venv .venv[m
[32m+[m[32m.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1[m
[32m+[m[32mpython -m pip install -r requirements.txt[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Model setup[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe default model is loaded from `results/checkpoint-3159`. This directory must[m
[32m+[m[32mcontain the saved model weights, configuration, and tokenizer files. Model weights[m
[32m+[m[32mare not included in Git, and installing requirements does not download this checkpoint.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mTo use another compatible local model, set its path before starting the app:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```powershell[m
[32m+[m[32m$env:EMAIL_MODEL_PATH = "C:\path\to\your\model"[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Gmail setup[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. Enable the Gmail API in your Google Cloud project.[m
[32m+[m[32m2. Configure your OAuth consent screen and a web application OAuth client.[m
[32m+[m[32m3. Register this redirect URI exactly:[m
[32m+[m[32m   `http://localhost:8000/auth/google/callback`.[m
[32m+[m[32m4. Save your OAuth client configuration as `credentials.json` in the project folder.[m
[32m+[m[32m5. Start the app and open `http://localhost:8000/auth/google` in your browser.[m
[32m+[m[32m6. Complete consent. The callback saves the local `token.json` file.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mIf the OAuth app is in testing mode, your Google account must be an allowed test user.[m
[32m+[m[32mUse `localhost` consistently when starting login and returning to the callback.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Run the app[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mRun this command from the project folder:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```powershell[m
[32m+[m[32mfastapi dev main.py[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAPI documentation: [Swagger UI](http://localhost:8000/docs).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Main endpoints[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| Method | Endpoint | Purpose |[m
[32m+[m[32m|---|---|---|[m
[32m+[m[32m| GET | `/` | Check that the API is running |[m
[32m+[m[32m| GET | `/auth/google` | Start Google login |[m
[32m+[m[32m| GET | `/auth/google/callback` | Complete OAuth and save credentials locally |[m
[32m+[m[32m| GET | `/gmail/messages` | Fetch and classify up to 5 Gmail messages |[m
[32m+[m[32m| POST | `/classify-email` | Classify a supplied subject and body |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mExample request for `POST /classify-email`:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```json[m
[32m+[m[32m{[m
[32m+[m[32m  "subject": "Interview invitation",[m
[32m+[m[32m  "body": "We would like to invite you for an interview on Monday."[m
[32m+[m[32m}[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mWhen messages are found, `GET /gmail/messages` returns `count`, `success_count`,[m
[32m+[m[32m`failed_count`, and `emails`. Successful entries include `id`, `from`, `date`,[m
[32m+[m[32m`subject`, `body`, and `predictions`. A failed entry includes its `id` and the[m
[32m+[m[32msafe message `"Failed to process email"`; remaining messages continue processing.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe current empty-inbox response is:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```json[m
[32m+[m[32m{"message": "No emails found"}[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Run tests[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mFrom the project folder:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```powershell[m
[32m+[m[32mpytest -v[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mGmail tests mock `routes.get_gmail_service`, extraction, and classification. They[m
[32m+[m[32mcover success, per-message failures, and empty responses without contacting Gmail.[m
[32m+[m[32mOAuth tests use synthetic credentials and mock the token exchange and token-file[m
[32m+[m[32mwrite. No Google login is required for tests. The existing API tests still load the[m
[32m+[m[32mlocal model, so the model files must be available.[m
[32m+[m
